MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
The M option makes a skip matched: while its closing delimiter is
being looked for, any skip name that turns up starts a nested skip and
is matched with its own delimiters first. Without M the skip is
straight, its own name inside it means nothing, and it ends at the
first closing delimiter that appears.
MCSKIP T,PLAIN;
MCSKIP MT,PAIRED;
PLAIN a PLAIN b; c; d
PAIRED a PAIRED b; c; d
A straight skip met inside a matched one is still matched first, so it
hides everything it swallows, a closing bracket included.
<one PLAIN two > three; four>
The delimiters of a nested skip arrive as ordinary text, because what
a nest keeps is settled by the outermost skip alone.
